# The image-scan suppression inventory (scripts/image-scan.mjs): committed, listed in suppressions.txt, and the
# only place a HIGH or CRITICAL vulnerability in the service image may be accepted. One entry per line,
# `<vulnerability id> exp:<yyyy-mm-dd>`, directly below a `#` line giving its reason; after the expiry trivy
# reports it again. Empty is the desired state. Prefer moving the base image digest in the Dockerfile to
# suppressing; an entry here is for a vulnerability with no fixed package in the base yet.
#
# Example:
# # no fixed package in trixie; the affected function is not reachable from the service
# # CVE-2026-0001 exp:2026-10-29
